Probably the number is on average more appropriate for the repeatedly
climbed stairs than for the actual throwback events (but see my numbers
below). After all, and to make the intention explicit, the round number
("40") should give a magnitude rather than being an actual count; once
I get The Amulet it wouldn't come to my mind to count every throwback
or stair climbed.

The point, though, was that the variance is so huge that you'll have to
be prepared to stay longer in Gehennom than you like and longer than you
have helpful ressources available (like scrolls of teleport to leave
quickly, or scrolls of remove curse, or holy water, or whatever else is
necessary). Any while even a (typically disadvantaged) lawful character
may escape quickly, don't expect that you escape with a chaotic character
faster; this difference can be so large that you need enough "breath" to
handle multiple appearances of Rodney and all the other already mentioned
bad effects. That difference is more significant than any self-controlled
delay that you may or may not want to take depending on the actual game.


